 "caveats": [
  "Global ice-volume equivalent, not relative sea level at a coast: glacial isostatic adjustment makes local sea level differ by up to tens of metres (near former ice sheets the land itself was depressed or uplifted).",
  "Present-day topography is used for past coastlines in the viewer; sedimentation, erosion, reef growth and tectonics since then are ignored.",
  "The 2-sigma band is Lambeck et al.'s accuracy estimate of the esl function, not the spread between different reconstructions (which is larger, e.g. LGM -120 to -135 m).",
  "Time steps are irregular (about 70-170 years); interpolate linearly between points."
